-- title:
--   Switcheroo Aggregate Target Eq Op Tensor Avg
-- statement:
--   **The target switcheroo aggregate equals the G-M tensor-product average.**
--
--   For an indexed polynomial family and indexed projective submeasurement `M`, the named target aggregate is exactly the uniform slice-pair average of the state expectation of the tensor product of the complete-part G total with the `M` total:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{switcherooAggregateTarget}(\mathrm{params},\psi_{bi},\mathrm{family},M)
--   =\mathbb E_q\,\operatorname{ev}_{\psi_{bi}}\!\left(\operatorname{opTensor}\left(G_{q.1}^{\mathrm{tot}},M_{q.2}^{\mathrm{tot}}\right)\right).
--   $$
--
--   This is an exact definition-level expansion over the uniform distribution on slice-pair questions. It supplies the target expression that the complete-part center and the commutativity switcheroo compare.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.switcherooAggregateTarget_eq_opTensor_avg`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
